  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Promoting university level skills and employability in the fields of emerging technologies in artificial intelligence and robotics in El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action intends to support curriculum development and skills in El Salvador in the areas of artificial intelligence (AI) and robotics, in line with the GGIA on digital connectivity and digital economy. This action will promote curricular development and labs for advanced technical degrees in the fields of prototype, robotics and mechatronics, virtual reality and AI, promoting capacity development for young people to develop advanced technological skills. Moreover, it will support the development of regulatory framework for AI. It will be implemented in direct management with the Institute for Innovation and Technology. The results will bring a new dimension to the TEI &#xbf;Digital Jobs&#xbf; focusing on development of digital skills in higher value-added sectors and promoting an AI regulatory framework inspired on the European model. The action is further supported by the Cybersecurity action of AAP 2024, working on regulatory framework and skills in cybersecurity. Improving the framework for better AI in El Salvador will have important cross-cutting positive impact on the country&#xbf;s digitalisation efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
